radare2
Usage: radare2 [-A] [-qc 'CMDS'] FILE

The reverse-engineering toolkit. `radare2` (alias `r2`) opens a binary in its
own interactive shell to disassemble, analyse and hex-edit it offline. The same
blob answers to sibling names: `rabin2` for headers, `rax2` for base conversion.

	r2 -A FILE       open and auto-analyse
	-qc 'CMDS' FILE  run commands and quit (scriptable, no shell)
	inside: afl (list functions), pdf @main (disasm), iz (strings), V (visual)
	rabin2 -I FILE   file headers -- type, arch, os
	rax2 0x41        convert between number bases

See also: r2, file, binwalk, strace
